course: dictionary
lesson: 11284
title: Written: on paper or spoken aloud?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Written is a word you will meet in many lessons, and it has a clear meaning: something is put down in words or numbers, on paper or on a screen. Look at the clues around it. «In written dialogue, speech marks go around the words spoken, and each new speaker starts a new line.» Dialogue means what characters say, and the speech marks show the words that are spoken. So written dialogue is dialogue that is put down on the page, not said out loud.
explain: The same idea works in school. A written test is done by writing answers, not by saying them. Ask yourself: is this something on paper or screen, or something said out loud? If you can picture it on a page, it is probably written.
explain: Written can also show who made something. «Written by» tells you the person who wrote a book or song. In a sentence like «The book was written by a famous author», the clue is by: it names the writer.
fact: Written means put down in words or numbers on paper or a screen.
fact: A written test or written answer is done by writing, not speaking.
fact: Write is the base word. Wrote is the past tense, and written is the word used after has or have, as in «She has written her name».
fact: In maths, left = total − written. If a book has 40 pages and 15 are written, then 40 − 15 = 25 pages are left.
fact: Phrases to know: written by, written down, written in, written test, the written word.
exercise: «In written dialogue, speech marks go around the words spoken.» What does written mean here? | Hidden under the bed | Spoken out loud | *Put down in words on paper or a screen | Drawn in pictures
exercise: A book has 40 pages and 15 pages are written. How many pages are left? | 15 | *25 | 55 | 40
exercise: Which one is a written test? | A quiz where the teacher asks you aloud | A chat about your favourite film | A game of hide and seek | *A spelling test where you write each word on paper
test: «The book was written by a famous author.» What does written by tell you? | Where the book was bought | How long the book is | *Who wrote the book
test: Which phrase means words put down on paper? | Silent word | Spoken word | Loud word | *The written word
exam: Mia has ___ her name at the top of the page. Which word fits? | writes | wrote | *written | writing
